(RAK HNT Miner Edition — Hyperfocus Zone Style)

1. WHY THIS MATTERS
The RAK HNT Miner is a Raspberry Pi 4 with a LoRa radio and special firmware, armored in metal.

Reliable setup/upgrade = Ethernet. Metal case = WiFi unreliable.

Network bridging (Laptop ↔ Pi) unlocks all maintenance, recovery, and empire upgrades!

2. MISSION GOAL
Bridge your laptop’s internet to the miner via Ethernet

Get the miner an IP address (192.168.137.x) so you can ping/SSH/manage it!

Celebrate with dopamine and BROski$ when it’s online!

3. TEAM-READY CHECKLIST
(Print, screenshot, or share in Discord/README!)

A. PREP & GEAR CHECK
☐ Power off miner

☐ Connect Ethernet (laptop <-> miner)

☐ Remove any WiFi dongles/adapters from miner

B. LAPTOP NETWORK CONFIG
☐ Open Network & Sharing Center > Change adapter settings

☐ Delete old network bridges

☐ Select WiFi + Ethernet > right-click > “Bridge Connections”

(If bridge fails: try Internet Connection Sharing instead!)

☐ Confirm Ethernet gets IP: 192.168.137.1 after bridging/sharing

C. POWER & BOOT
☐ Power on miner

☐ WAIT 3-5 mins (miner is slow to handshake)

☐ Watch red/green LEDs for boot status

D. NETWORK TEST
☐ Open PowerShell/CMD on laptop

☐ Run: arp -a (look for 192.168.137.x device)

☐ Try: ping 192.168.137.2

☐ If ping works, try: ssh pi@192.168.137.2 (or default RAK login)

E. HDMI CHECK (IF STUCK)
☐ Plug miner into monitor/TV via HDMI

☐ Look for boot messages, login prompt, or IP address on screen

4. STILL NOT WORKING?
☐ Try another cable/port!

☐ Confirm bridge is active & you have IPv4.

☐ Reboot both devices after network config changes.

☐ If all else fails:

☐ Reflash SD card with latest firmware

☐ Connect directly to router/switch for DHCP

5. RAK MINER PRO TIPS
Default login:

User: pi

Pass: raspberry (or check docs/custom firmware)

No SSH? Try Helium app + Bluetooth onboarding.

MAX rewards: Place >300 m from other hotspots.

